IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-interpretation`
IMPORT `sgf-s216a`

-- Tests for sgf-s216a.l4 (s 216A, derivative or representative actions).
-- Every expected value below was written from the text of s 216A (src:21782-21857 of CoA1967.txt) before the module was run,
-- never copied from its output. A failing assertion is a finding. Each rule is tried on both sides of each of its conditions.

§ `s 216A(1): who is a complainant`

-- Arguments: the body is a company incorporated under this Act; ... under a corresponding previous written law; the person is a member;
-- the person is the Minister; the company is a declared company under Part 9; the Court's view of the person (paragraph (c)).

-- (a) any member of a company.
#ASSERT `s 216A(1) the person is a complainant` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not treated the person as a proper person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) a member of a company incorporated under a corresponding previous written law: "company" covers it (s 4(1)).
#ASSERT `s 216A(1) the person is a complainant` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not treated the person as a proper person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A member whose company is a company, and the Court has not yet decided anything: paragraph (a) holds on its own.
#ASSERT `s 216A(1) the person is a complainant` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not yet decided` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) the Minister, in the case of a declared company under Part 9.
#ASSERT `s 216A(1) the person is a complainant` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not treated the person as a proper person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Minister, where the company is not a declared company, and the Court has not treated the Minister as a proper person: none holds.
#ASSERT `s 216A(1) the person is a complainant` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not treated the person as a proper person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) any other person whom the Court, in its discretion, treats as a proper person.
#ASSERT `s 216A(1) the person is a complainant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has treated the person as a proper person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Another person whom the Court has decided is not a proper person: the definition says no.
#ASSERT `s 216A(1) the person is a complainant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not treated the person as a proper person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Another person where the Court has not yet decided: the text points to a decision not yet made; not covered, never FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 216A(1) the person is a complainant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not yet decided` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A person holding shares by transmission who is not a member: s 216(7) speaks of "this section" (s 216) only, so s 216A(1)(a) does not
-- treat the person as a member; whether the person is a complainant is for the Court under (c): not yet decided, so not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216A(1) the person is a complainant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not yet decided` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A "member" of a body that is not a company: paragraph (a) does not hold; the Court has not treated the person as proper: no.
#ASSERT `s 216A(1) the person is a complainant` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not treated the person as a proper person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same, where the Court has treated the person as proper: paragraph (c) holds.
#ASSERT `s 216A(1) the person is a complainant` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has treated the person as a proper person` EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `s 216A(2): the application for permission`

-- Arguments: the person is a complainant; what the application is for.
#ASSERT `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission` TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission` TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an arbitration in the name and on behalf of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission` TRUE `s 216A(2) to intervene in an action to which the company is a party, to prosecute, defend or discontinue it on behalf of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission` TRUE `s 216A(2) to intervene in an arbitration to which the company is a party, to prosecute, defend or discontinue it on behalf of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Some other purpose: outside the four the grant names; not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission` TRUE `s 216A(2) for some other purpose` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A person who is not a complainant: outside the grant; not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission` FALSE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 216A(3)(a): 14 days' notice to the directors`

-- Arguments: the number of directors; the number of directors notified; the notice stated the intention to apply if the directors do
-- not act; the date the notice was given; the date the complainant applies.

-- Notice given on 1 March 2027 to all three directors, application on 15 March 2027, exactly 14 days later: in time.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- One day later: in time.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 16 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- One day short (13 days): not 14 days' notice; the "unless" condition is not met.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 14 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The application on the day of the notice: no notice period at all.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A notice dated after the application: not notice before it.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` 3 3 TRUE (Date 20 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Only two of the three directors notified.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` 3 2 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The notice does not say what the complainant intends.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` 3 3 FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A company with only one director (s 4(10)): notice to that director is notice to "the directors".
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` 1 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` 1 0 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No director at all, and none notified: there is no notice to "the directors" to speak of.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` 0 0 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Across the end of February 2027 (28 days): notice 20 February, application 6 March is the 14th day; 5 March is the 13th.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` 2 2 TRUE (Date 20 2 2027) (Date 6 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` 2 2 TRUE (Date 20 2 2027) (Date 5 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Across the end of February 2028 (29 days): notice 25 February, application 10 March is the 14th day; 9 March is the 13th.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` 2 2 TRUE (Date 25 2 2028) (Date 10 3 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` 2 2 TRUE (Date 25 2 2028) (Date 9 3 2028) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The latest day for the notice, given the day of the application.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the latest day on which the complainant can give the directors notice` (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS Date 1 3 2027
-- Across the end of the year: apply on 5 January 2027, the notice must be given by 22 December 2026.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the latest day on which the complainant can give the directors notice` (Date 5 1 2027) EQUALS Date 22 12 2026
-- Leap year: apply on 10 March 2028, the notice must be given by 25 February 2028.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the latest day on which the complainant can give the directors notice` (Date 10 3 2028) EQUALS Date 25 2 2028
-- The earliest day for the application, given the day of the notice.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the earliest day on which the complainant can apply to the Court` (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS Date 15 3 2027
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the earliest day on which the complainant can apply to the Court` (Date 22 12 2026) EQUALS Date 5 1 2027
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(a) the earliest day on which the complainant can apply to the Court` (Date 25 2 2028) EQUALS Date 10 3 2028

§ `s 216A(3)(b) and (c): good faith, and prima facie in the interests of the company`

#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(b) the complainant is acting in good faith` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(b) the complainant is acting in good faith` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(c) it appears to be prima facie in the interests of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216A(3)(c) it appears to be prima facie in the interests of the company` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 216A(3): the bar, as a whole`

-- Arguments: the action is under s 216A(2); the number of directors; the number notified; the notice stated the intention; the date of
-- the notice; the date of the application; the complainant is acting in good faith; it appears to be prima facie in the company's interests.

-- All three conditions are met: the "unless" is satisfied, so the bar does not apply (it does not say permission is granted).
#ASSERT `s 216A(3) the bar on bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, applies` TRUE 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Notice one day short: the bar applies.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3) the bar on bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, applies` TRUE 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 14 3 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not acting in good faith: the bar applies.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3) the bar on bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, applies` TRUE 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not prima facie in the interests of the company: the bar applies.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3) the bar on bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, applies` TRUE 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not all the directors notified: the bar applies.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3) the bar on bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, applies` TRUE 3 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- All three fail: the bar applies.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3) the bar on bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, applies` TRUE 3 0 FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An action outside subsection (2) (for instance at common law): the bar speaks of "under subsection (2)" only; not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3) the bar on bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, applies` FALSE 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216A(3) the bar on bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, applies` FALSE 3 0 FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A company with one director, notified, all else met: the bar does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 216A(3) the bar on bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, applies` TRUE 1 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 216A(4): the interim order where notice is not expedient`

#ASSERT `s 216A(4) the Court may make an interim order pending the complainant giving notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The "where" condition is not met (split site (ii): JUST FALSE by the periods ruling (b); the other reading is NOTHING).
#ASSERT `s 216A(4) the Court may make an interim order pending the complainant giving notice` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 216A(5): orders in granting permission`

-- Arguments: the Court is granting permission under s 216A.
#ASSERT `s 216A(5) the Court may make the orders or interim orders it thinks fit in the interests of justice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216A(5) the Court may make the orders or interim orders it thinks fit in the interests of justice` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216A(5)(a) the Court may make an order authorising the complainant or any other person to control the conduct of the action or arbitration` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216A(5)(a) the Court may make an order authorising the complainant or any other person to control the conduct of the action or arbitration` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b): the Court is granting permission; a person has been authorised to control the conduct.
#ASSERT `s 216A(5)(b) the Court may make an order giving directions for the conduct of the action or arbitration by the person so authorised` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216A(5)(b) the Court may make an order giving directions for the conduct of the action or arbitration by the person so authorised` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216A(5)(b) the Court may make an order giving directions for the conduct of the action or arbitration by the person so authorised` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c): the Court is granting permission; the fees are reasonable; they were incurred by the complainant in connection with the action.
#ASSERT `s 216A(5)(c) the Court may make an order requiring the company to pay the complainant's legal fees and disbursements` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216A(5)(c) the Court may make an order requiring the company to pay the complainant's legal fees and disbursements` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216A(5)(c) the Court may make an order requiring the company to pay the complainant's legal fees and disbursements` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216A(5)(c) the Court may make an order requiring the company to pay the complainant's legal fees and disbursements` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 216A(6): the State Courts`

#ASSERT `s 216A(6) the application for permission is required to be made in a District Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216A(6) the application for permission is required to be made in a District Court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
